<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Odendaal Plan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1964</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Odendaal Plan was a scheme for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">South West Africa</a> (Namibia) proposed in 1964 by a South African commission under Frans Hendrik Odendaal. It applied apartheid's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> policy to the territory, dividing it into ethnic homelands for the black population and a larger area for whites, and was put into effect from the late 1960s. The plan was condemned by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> and by the liberation movement <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swapo">SWAPO</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/odendaal-plan.jpg" alt="Odendaal Plan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bries · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plan_Odendaal.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
